{
  "name": "visual-capture",
  "kind": "flow",
  "title": "What a capture stores, and where",
  "desc": "The capture driver reads the local app's page in a temporary folder that it deletes afterward, and hands its picture, text, and check signals to redaction in memory. Only after redaction does anything reach the disk: pictures and descriptions go to the local store on this Mac, and the text records go to the handoff repository. Form values, cookies, and storage are never stored.",
